# Language Standard (EN active · LT frozen)

**Policy:** Active development is **English only**. Edit shipped copy in **`src/content/locales/en.ts`** (re-exported via `src/content/copy.ts`), EN UI fallbacks in `src/components/**/*.astro`, English prose in `public/assets/downloads/`, and project docs. **Do not update Lithuanian strings** in **`lt.ts`** unless the user explicitly unfreezes bilingual delivery.

`lt.ts` remains in the repo as a **frozen archive** (no `/lt/` route ships by default). Do not run LT prose audits or maintain EN/LT parity during normal work.

## Shared Principles

- Executive voice: decision, risk, trade-off, owner, next action, ROI.
- Forbidden vocabulary in marketing copy: "learn AI", "prompt engineering tutorial", "AI course", "beginner guide", "step-by-step intro".
- One idea per sentence. Cut adjectives that do not change meaning.
- No emoji in landing copy unless explicitly requested by the user.
- Brand names stay verbatim: `PromptAnatomy`, `PromptAnatomy.app`, `Max Value Kit`.

## Quick gate (copy edits)

- User-visible changes go in **`en.ts`** (or EN component fallbacks) only.
- Shipped EN uses American English (see US table below).
- No beginner-AI vocabulary in marketing copy.
- If you **add or remove locale keys** in `en.ts`, add matching keys in `lt.ts` with **English placeholder strings** so `localeParity.test.ts` passes — do not translate into Lithuanian while LT is frozen.
- Full completion bar → [`docs/DEFINITION_OF_DONE.md`](../../docs/DEFINITION_OF_DONE.md).

## English Standard

### Voice

- Sentence case for headings and CTAs: `Download Max Value Kit`, not `Download Max Value KIT` or `Download max value kit`.
- Active voice. `The kit returns a decision-ready output` ✓ over `A decision-ready output is returned by the kit` ✗.
- Cut hedges: `helps you to`, `aims to`, `tries to`. State the outcome.
- Numbers under 10 spelled out only in body prose; in metric chips use digits (`2min`, `35`, `7`).

### Vocabulary

| Prefer | Avoid |
|---|---|
| decision, trade-off, risk, owner | insight, synergy, leverage (as a noun) |
| executive, leadership team | C-suite, leadership cadre |
| operating kit | playbook (overused) |
| safety check | guardrails (when speaking to CEOs) |
| install the system | onboard the system |

### Punctuation

- Em dash `—` (no spaces) for emphatic asides: `Decision first — every prompt points to an owner.`
- Oxford comma in lists of three or more.
- Sentence ends with one period only; no `..` or `...` unless quoting.

### US English (shipped default)

The default USA-market build uses **American English** in all **user-visible** English: **`src/content/locales/en.ts`**, **`public/**` marketing copy** where prose is shown to visitors (e.g. printable kit body text), and English UI strings in components. Do not ship UK spellings or UK-only connectives into those surfaces.

International B2B terms that read the same in US executive copy (**Q3**, **ARR**, **runway**, **board deck**) stay as-is. **UK-preferred spellings and wording** do not belong in shipped `en`.

| Use (US) | Avoid in shipped EN (UK) |
|---|---|
| behavior, organization, analyze, center, license (n.), defense, labeling, modeling | behaviour, organisation, analyse, centre, licence (n.), defence, labelling, modelling |
| while, among | whilst, amongst |
| practice (v. and n.) | practise (verb) |

Technical layers follow platform spelling (e.g. CSS `color`, DOM “behavior” in APIs)—that is not marketing copy and is out of scope for this rule.

## English audit checklist

When asked to audit English copy:

- [ ] No beginner-AI vocabulary.
- [ ] Headings in sentence case.
- [ ] No passive voice on key value statements.
- [ ] Each prompt category description names a decision, risk, trade-off, or next action.
- [ ] No UK-preferred spellings in user-visible `en` strings (see **US English (shipped default)** table above).
- [ ] No UK-only connectives/phrasing where US reads more natural (`whilst`, `amongst`, etc.).

After substantive copy edits, follow [`docs/DEFINITION_OF_DONE.md`](../../docs/DEFINITION_OF_DONE.md) (build, test, CHANGELOG).

## Lithuanian archive (frozen — do not edit)

`src/content/locales/lt.ts` is **not maintained**. Unfreeze only when product re-enables bilingual delivery (see root `README.md` — Locale toggle) and explicitly asks for LT work.

Reference material if unfreezing later:

- Address: **Tu** (not Jūs); buttons use infinitive labels.
- **DI** (not AI) in Lithuanian copy.
- Mandatory diacritics: `ą č ę ė į š ų ū ž`.
- Long dash `–` for emphasis; preferred business vocabulary (`kompromisas`, `butelio kaklelis`, `darbo eiga`, `promptas`).

Do not apply LT rules during EN-only development.
